# Note on the systemd/README.md "CLOSED SET of 19" STANDING RULE in this
# same directory: that rule scopes explicitly to *periodic* cron-replacement
# units (OnCalendar timer + oneshot service pairs standing in for the old
# crontab). This unit is not periodic -- Type=simple, Restart=always, no
# .timer pairing, WantedBy=default.target (starts once at login and runs
# continuously) -- the same shape as veridian-directive-engine.service
# itself and veridian-worker@.service, both of which are real live units on
# this box and neither of which is part of that closed set for the same
# reason. It therefore does not fall under that STANDING RULE and does not
# need a 20th-cron-unit exception the way
# systemd/veridian-cron-prune-memory-backups.* did.
#
# Authorization: this is a real mechanical-blocker dispatch
# (task-20260806-230715, PM report contract UMR-20260806-042531-be9c) whose
# own explicit step 2 instructs "enabling a real systemd audit mechanism
# that captures the real job origin" as one of two named acceptable
# mechanisms -- the dispatch instruction is itself the explicit decision
# authorizing this one companion unit, same precedent already used for the
# memory-backup-prune exception in systemd/README.md's "Unit #20" section.
# Registered under child UMR-20260806-231410-331d (insert-owner-proposal,
# pm_decisions_pending id=295), linked under parent UMR-20260806-103954-6f42.
#
# WHY this mechanism over a plain ExecStop= hook on the target unit, and the
# honest limitation discovered while building it: see the header comment of
# /opt/veridian/scripts/directive-engine-stop-audit-monitor.sh (this unit's
# real ExecStart=), which documents both in full, including a live
# self-test result and a documented, abandoned 2nd approach (a
# dbus-python persistent-connection daemon,
# directive_engine_stop_audit_monitor.py, kept in this repo for the record
# but NOT wired to this unit after a reproducible crash -- 2 consecutive
# failures of that approach, stopped per this task's own protocol rather
# than reattempted a 3rd time).
# =============================================================================
[Unit]
Description=VERIDIAN real-time D-Bus audit: captures the real caller of StopUnit/KillUnit/RestartUnit/Unit.Stop against veridian-directive-engine.service (UMR-20260806-231410-331d, child of UMR-20260806-103954-6f42)
After=default.target

[Service]
ExecStart=/opt/veridian/scripts/directive-engine-stop-audit-monitor.sh
Restart=always
RestartSec=2

[Install]
WantedBy=default.target
